    "schemaRule": "Every object follows its $defs required and properties insertion order, exactly. Const arrays compare elementwise in supplied order; transport canonical ASCII dates and occurrence joining are separate. The schema checks wire shape and constants; enforce relational rules below separately. Generic JSON Schema ignores key order. A structural validator alone cannot admit this protocol.",
    "artifactConsistency": "Only two normal frames in this order, emitted once after all checks/own cleanup. Embedded custody must byte-match the first frame body. Prepare both complete canonical frames/payload before emitting normal markers. On infrastructure failure use FAULT with failing command and no admissible artifact; never accept partial line, success pair + FAULT, a partial pair, upload failure, or mixing occurrences. If physical transport fails before fault can be produced, the unique occurrence still fails admission.",
