  "identity": {
    "gitSource": "Before executing, verify original 3203 BASE leaf modes/blob IDs and exact additional DATA edges per inventory. BASE absence at canonical S08 and legacy S09 there is correct. Bind all 13 canonical afterimages only in owned materialized target, plus separately sealed D07 and recorder. Compute bytes/SHA256 and Git blob for each real target canonical file before GREEN and again after child exit/timeout before cleanup. Each projection is an independently built ordered list of 13 SHA256 values recorded in sourceReads.beforeSha256 and sourceReads.afterSha256. Neither may be filled from the index or copied from the other. Bind lengths/git IDs both times locally and independently to immutable normal-13 Git DATA tree. OWN demands both arrays exactly equal index rows and tree edges. Mismatch or inability to read -> infrastructure failure; no successful observation.",
    "manifest": "Verify raw selection artifact git/bytes/sha vs p(selection), independently compute selectionWireHash from compact UTF8 JSON.stringify(selection) WITHOUT LF. Bind exact D07 sibling in argv and stack alias, S07 still canonical; seal actual pinned D07 bytes, one-alias projected recorder, journal reader. Reject reverse alias/legacy driver path, mixed bodyhash, fake complete claim or old green manifest/job. No new callbacks, remount strategy, original clocks, test predicates or additional native business calls.",
    "activeIndex": "Current Source13 is unchanged from accepted TOOL inputs. Its 13 entries bind carrier afterimages in order. S08–S10 keep their exact inert dataPath entries from the immutable index."
  },
  "custody": "Exactly two checked native launches: owned-file preflight under ten seconds THEN all twenty GREEN cases in one process launch with normal compiled fixtures. No synthetic battery/ENOENT/BASE/mutant/regression/N3/W1 in capture. Together share a single target; each observed >=1 fresh unique PID record, retain all previous, union<=8. preflightProcesses and greenProcesses are separate actual fresh counts at each launch; checkedProcesses = their sum (2..8); no invented values. Parent positive UID, child exact UID/GID, cleared supplementary groups and loopback-only, sudo unshare + setpriv --no-new-privs, exact guard before native target, fresh regular safe files. Use existing 0600/single-link/no-symlink/ownership/dev/inode/size checks for journal and scoped temp creation/removal. `uidGidGroupsLoopbackMatched` reports observed guard facts; the `--no-new-privs` launch flag is bound to reviewed runner. `journalOwnershipMatched` and two target booleans mean actual readings succeeded, prior preflight/temp removal confirmed. Maximum custody body with longest admitted runId remains within 1024 bytes.",
  "capture": "Capture from actual returned spawnSync object only, using existing finite safeCapture. Require observed stdout/stderr buffers within caps, measured bytes and SHA256. ETIMEDOUT ⇒ errorKind:'timeout'; keep independently returned numeric status or null and finite signals as frozen mapping (null=>'none'; known names literal; unrecognized string=>'other'; unavailable=>'unavailable'). Never set status=1/HANG by inference. When errorKind:'none' require signal:'none' and exitCode 0 or 1. Other spawn/err/signal combinations, overflow/missing streams/ownership/incorrect argv ⇒ infrastructure FAULT. Artifact marks diagnosticCollectionComplete:true and nativeQualification:false for collected exit0, native exit1 or ETIMEDOUT; original child condition stays visible. No eligibility/Source proof from job success. Require exact standard SHA256(empty) whenever byte count is zero.",
  "journal": {
    "physical": "Fresh parent-created exclusive blank 0600 file/O_NOFOLLOW/expected device+inode/owner/nlink. Recorder opens, appends one canonical LF-terminated row, closes synchronously, has no extra active timer. Read via same identity checked fd in RAM after child; before/after stats and read length agree; oversize/short read/identity/symlink/nonstable storage => FAULT,never a sanitized stable prefix claim. Raw journal <=32768 B/128 rows. Export validated rows only. Clamp by rejecting invalid data; never clip a valid finite value into range.",
    "intervals": "Each complete canonical row parsed from exact bytes has sequence starting 1 and +1, elapsedMs 0..330000 nondecreasing, error:null for enter/return; on throw exact error object with allowlist name/code and exact reduced alias+line/column or null. Unknown error details stay null. For 20 nominal IDs, in order: action enter→return|throw, count enter→return|throw, then next id. AFTER close independent enter→return|throw at most once, may overlap any case. A missing world means D07 does not record a counter it never called; do not fabricate one or skip missing intervals to recover later. Records stop at first semantically invalid/malformed row. Select 62a31 progress() behavior including suppressing frontier on torn/ambiguous, and nativePrefix() separately.",
    "integrity": "Complete/prefix/empty clean journals require equality of raw byte length and SHA256 against the concatenation UTF8(JSON.stringify(event)+'\\n') for all exported rows. Stable torn/invalid tail has rawBytes strictly larger than canonical validated prefix size (raw tail not exported); observed-recorder-fault can occur with zero tail. For any integrity, if lengths equal, require raw digest equal reconstructed prefix digest. For stable torn/invalid with unexported suffix, full raw digest is a bounded producer observation; do not claim independent proof of bytes not supplied. Preserve stable recorder-fault indication observed in actual stdout/stderr; false only means marker not observed. Ambiguous/invalid marker from the *binding* is fatal; malformed alias in a stable individual event is truncated before that event and yields UNKNOWN.",
    "unknown": "If recorderFaultObserved=true, witness.integrity='ambiguous' and unknownReason='RECORDER_FAULT' (also if an invalid/torn record is present). Else if the first unaccepted complete record is invalid (including invalid alias), integrity='ambiguous', reason='JOURNAL_INVALID_RECORD'. Else if any incomplete final line follows valid complete rows, integrity='torn', reason='JOURNAL_TORN'. Else if no data, integrity='empty', reason='JOURNAL_EMPTY'. All four set frontier='unknown',openCase=null,afterOpen=false, where null/false are protocol sentinels and cannot establish absence. Preserve valid preceding rows and native evidence independently. For prefix or complete require unknownReason=null, stable true and no recorder fault.",
    "frontier": "For known journal, use exact legacy frontier labels and recompute from chronological events. At complete all20 case actions/count and AFTER closed, timeout plus any throw ⇒ post-settlement-process-exit, without throw ⇒ post-teardown-process-exit, else normal end ⇒ all-settled. With case & after open ⇒ case-and-after; else case action or count, else after-close, else between-action-and-count after action end, else before-after for all20 finished/AFTER unopened, else between-cases. `firstThrowSequence` is the earliest edge='throw' within the validated contiguous exported prefix, including AFTER, else null. This is a pointer to an observed record, not a verdict about missing history. Never designate last absolute event or process/physical hold from torn tail."
  },
  "nativeAndCross": "Use exact published LF-terminated serial top-level TAP result lines paired to corresponding Subtest, ordinal and expected exact ID; never promote C2SOURCE/unterminated line or conflate journal and native. Preserved nativePrefix62a31 results use prefix/empty/torn/ambiguous only; prefix can contain all20 without exporting complete native TAP totals. Empty => zero observed pairs; ambiguous/torn may contain only previously complete pairs. Do not invent evidence after first ambiguity. Do not claim unconditional worker settlement. For every observed native pass, any stable validated action/count throw of the SAME id is a contradiction (N2), even if later journal tail is unknown. Other id/global AFTER throw is not the same contradiction. A TAP fail need not have a journal throw (framework/timeouts exist). Alias allowlist bound to exact temp file/URL, exact source or D07 path, bounds per schema; no suffix matches.",
  "transport": "Prebind raw tree/body/nomination before push. Receiver independently joins repo/event push/head/parent/tree/ref/message, logical job, seven-minute workflow and attempt1 to actual API unique terminal job ID and actual command-step number. All six actual required steps succeed in order for accepted diagnostic; if run/step is incomplete, preserve what actually occurred as partial separately. N1: unique timestamped ##[group]Run <exact command>, finite times on header and each marker within actual command window ±1000ms per existing N1, header closed by ##[endgroup] before stdout and before next step group. Reject malformed/smuggled/mixed duplicate markers even outside selected window, archived API job with misleading same names, artifacts outside this head/branch/run. Bind ordered pair plus canonical outcome JSON+LF to actual ZIP compressed bytes/digest/listing/entry count/name, ownership/time, exact CRC/size/full deflate consumption and closed primitive from OWN419. Reuse OWN independent logic only, never producer helper or imported Source oracle.",
  "fault": {
    "meaning": "Missing immutable wire/target alias, admission/custody failure, unstable owned read, process capture outside defined combinations, N2/contract conflict or failed cleanup/publication => reject. An actual fault during collection, once captured, emits only finite fault marker if reporting possible, exits nonzero, no eligible artifact. Stable incomplete evidence reasons in journal.unknown are collected; do not send FAULT just because the original child timed out or a record was torn. The `RECORDER_FAULT` reason in FAULT envelope is reserved for a failure to establish a trustworthy recorder/transport identity or fault classification; a stable orderly observed flag inside approved target is handled by the success envelope with uncertain frontier.",
    "phaseReasons": {
      "admission": [
        "ADMISSION_INVALID"
      ],
      "materialize": [
        "MATERIALIZATION_INVALID",
        "TARGET_DRIFT"
      ],
      "preflight": [
        "PREFLIGHT_INVALID",
        "CUSTODY_INVALID"
      ],
      "green": [
        "LAUNCH_INVALID",
        "CUSTODY_INVALID",
        "CAPTURE_INVALID"
      ],
      "journal": [
        "JOURNAL_INVALID",
        "RECORDER_FAULT",
        "TARGET_DRIFT"
      ],
      "native": [
        "CAPTURE_INVALID",
        "EVIDENCE_CONFLICT"
      ],
      "cleanup": [
        "CLEANUP_INVALID",
        "TARGET_DRIFT"
      ],
      "publish": [
        "PUBLICATION_INVALID"
      ]
    },
    "context": "null only if admission failed before context could be established; valid pinned context mandatory after admission. No secret/raw/error stack in fault."
  },
  "firstFailure": {
    "definition": "#/$defs/firstFailure",
    "componentCanonicalSha256": "012c2fcc1bc208fea6a442d798577f5668e2dec7e96c61eae44ccc6218a8545d",
    "mandatory": true,
    "bodyBytesMax": 512,
    "scope": "Capacidad opcional por selección explícita de familia nueva; DIAG1 heredado queda inmutable y rechaza campos nuevos. En DIAG2 firstFailure es obligatorio y emite UNKNOWN/NOT_APPLICABLE explícitos cuando corresponda; ausencia no equivale a UNKNOWN válido. No field silenciosamente opcional dentro de la nueva versión.",
    "outputOnly": "Sólo firstFailure6keys; KNOWN contiene source canonical5keys y assertion2ints. UNKNOWN/NOT_APPLICABLE tienen throwSequence/source/assertion null. Los hechos ya disponibles permanecen sin cambios en outer journal/native; null no borra ni niega esos hechos.",
    "sourceProjection": {
      "inputs": "Mismos child.stdout Buffer ya capturado y sus sha/bytes, observación journal validada por readProgress y nativePrefix heredados, selección20 y contexto/pins fijados. Incluso ETIMEDOUT se inspecciona el buffer existente; no nueva lectura de proceso/servicio ni source hook.",
      "output": "Sólo firstFailure6keys; KNOWN contiene source canonical5keys y assertion2ints. UNKNOWN/NOT_APPLICABLE tienen throwSequence/source/assertion null. Los hechos ya disponibles permanecen sin cambios en outer journal/native; null no borra ni niega esos hechos.",
      "knownCandidate": [
        "El prefijo journal exportado se valida desde seq1 sin huecos; su primera edge throw dentro de ese prefijo es idC2T1_NOTICES,operationaction,error.nameAssertionError,codeERR_ASSERTION,siteS08:41:12. No utilizar una throw posterior ni buscar el target saltando una anterior.",
        "Los11 casos previos actuales del mismo prefijo tienen action/countreturn y los11 nativepairs actuales PASS en orden; native[11] es exactamente fail C2T1_NOTICES con ordinal12 top-level y sin skip/todo. No heredar estos hechos de DIAG1/historia.",
        "El target tiene su count.enter y count.return completos tras la action.throw, sin countthrow. Estos hechos pueden estar en un prefijo conservado de journal luego torn/ambiguous/recorder-fault; no se requiere recuperar ni afirmar el sufijo privado. Si el propio candidato o su counter no están cerrados, UNKNOWN.",
        "Un único C2SOURCE target canonical id/status/phase/counters/code exactos, fail/notices/TEST_FAILED y counters0..3 enteros; se extrae del stdout en su envoltura real TAP '# C2SOURCE '. El prefijo SourceRows aceptado hasta target debe concordar con orden20 y las filas precedentes presentes, sin duplicados, saltos ni reorden. El extractor no pide ni exporta un beforeEXTRA_KEY.",
        "Único bloque diagnóstico estructural del par nativo12, completo y cerrado, con failureType testCodeFailure,codeERR_ASSERTION,nameAssertionError,operatorstrictEqual. Sólo scalars mapping al nivel2espacios expected200 y actualint100..599 distinto200; no mensajes/stack/location como fuente de status. El bloque pertenece al result12; SourceRow se enlaza por ID/orden propio, sin adyacencia ni orden físico relativo aSubtest.",
        "La gramática física de las envolturas console y diagnostic debe haber sido calibrada y sellada por toy Node22.23.4 con await work()/awaitcounts()/catch/rethrow. No imponer SourceRow/Subtest adyacentes ni un orden físico relativo; mantener SourceRows ordenados por selectedIDs y pares/bloques nativos por ordinal/ID, site de journal. No ampliar tolerancias a ciegas si difiere del sello; STOP o UNKNOWN. Context/source/helper pins caller expectation exactos."
      ],
      "prefixUnknownSuffix": "Root ruling: un sufijo posterior torn/unknown no deshace un candidato completo y validado. En ese caso KNOWN significa first throw del prefijo validado; nunca globallyearliest, drenaje o integridad de bytes no exportados. Se conservan integrity/unknownReason/firstThrowSequence outer originales.",
      "sourceCounters": "Sólo bounds heredados0..3, sin receipts<=activation<=upload inventado, monotonicidad, delta, forzar2/2/2 ni cero por default. Los counters son las tres medidas post-action de D07:18 y no prueban causalidad, autenticidad de receipt ni completitud M/QA.",
      "rawGrammar": [
        "Parseo delimitado de LF UTF8 canónico; sin YAML general ni deps. Nativepairs se enlazan a Subtest top-level exacto yordinal, manteniendo gramática flat y parser heredado independiente. El bloque del target pertenece exclusivamente a su result y delimitadores '  ---'/'  ...'. SourceRows C2SOURCE se enlazan por ID y orden de selectedIDs, nunca por adyacencia física al Subtest ni posición relativa entre esas dos corrientes. No capturar bloque posterior o anidado.",
        "Dentro del bloque sólo los campos top-level2espacios pueden aportar scalars. Textos de error/stack y su indent4+ son opacos y se descartan; un actual/expected falso allí no cuenta. Datos unsupported/tabs/CR/bloqueabierto o scalarambiguo son UNKNOWN, no coerción.",
        "No strings numéricos, floats/exponente/hex/NaN/Infinity/null/boolean/arrays/maps; actual200 o expected distinto200 contradicen esta aserción y son UNKNOWN CONFLICTING_EVIDENCE. Duplicados de scalar/source/par,ordinal/case/site erróneos,nesting/source keyorder no canónico/reorden no producen KNOWN. Un mapping anidado o texto opaco se ignora para scalars, no se promueve ni se usa como fallback.",
        "Escanear el buffer ya acotado para duplicados/fakes relevantes; no cerrar el scan tras el primer valor válido. Descartar copias de C2SOURCE dentro de YAML/comments escapados, stack o nested TAP. Una falsificación estructural no se promueve aunque el númeroparezca plausible.",
        "Timeout global no equivale a truncación del candidato: prefijo nativo19 limpio con target12/bloque completos puede KNOWN aunque20sigaabierto. TRUNCATED_NATIVE se refiere al candidato/gramática relevante no cerrados o un sufijo ambiguo que impide unicidad, no a la mera ausencia de20/TAPtotals."
      ],
      "reasonPriority": [
        "0: Fallos heredados de API/contexto/tree/pins/transporte/custody/N2 impiden admisión y siguen FAULT; nunca normalizarlos medianteUNKNOWN.",
        "1: Primera throw fiable en el prefijo validado con id/op/name/code/site diferente del candidato exacto ⇒ NOT_APPLICABLE EARLIEST_THROW_DIFFERENT. Unknownsuffix posterior no borra esa prueba; no significa primerfalloglobal.",
        "2: Pareja native previa a12 FAIL inequívoca ⇒ NOT_APPLICABLE EARLIER_NATIVE_FAILURE. TargetPASS inequívoco más action/countreturn12 validados ⇒ NOT_APPLICABLE TARGET_PASSED. Si faltan las pruebas journal de ese PASS por un corte, UNKNOWN JOURNAL_UNRESOLVED.",
        "3: NO_QUALIFYING_THROW sólo con journal cleancomplete20+AFTER y ausencia de throws: NOT_APPLICABLE. Nunca inferir ausencia desde un prefijo cortado/unknown. Sin candidato comprobado en el prefijo ⇒ UNKNOWN JOURNAL_UNRESOLVED.",
        "4: Para un exactcandidate comprobado, countthrow/count no cerrado ⇒ UNKNOWN COUNTER_UNAVAILABLE. Más allá de eso, bytes/grammarrelevante cortados ⇒ TRUNCATED_NATIVE; CR/UTF8 o layout no calibrado ⇒ NATIVE_FORMAT_UNSUPPORTED; native pair/ordinal/duplicados/reorden ambiguos ⇒ AMBIGUOUS_EVIDENCE; targetpair ausente ⇒ TARGET_NATIVE_UNAVAILABLE.",
        "5: SourceRow o campo estructural relevante duplicado/nested falso/no canónico/reorden ⇒ AMBIGUOUS_EVIDENCE; contradicción de campos conocidos ⇒ CONFLICTING_EVIDENCE; SourceRow ausente ⇒ SOURCE_ROW_UNAVAILABLE; expected/actual top-level faltante (incluso sólo fake anidado/message/stack) ⇒ ASSERTION_SCALARS_UNAVAILABLE; tipo/rango no soportado ⇒ UNSUPPORTED_SCALARS. Primero aplicar estas categorías a SourceRow y luego al bloque assertion; nunca rescatar un valor entre duplicados.",
        "6: Sólo todos los joins completos ⇒ KNOWN TARGET_POST_ASSERTION. throwSequence igual al outerfirstThrowSequence dentro del prefijovalidado. Journalunknown posterior no lo deshace si el candidato/count y todos sus antecedentes necesarios ya estaban completos."
      ],
      "forbiddenExport": "No RAWactualTAP, message/stack/location/URLs/paths absolutos/formularios/handles/cookies/SQL/D1/providerrows/arbitrarystrings fuera del parent. Error metadata previa sigue su allowlist. SHAstdout bindea bytes capturados pero no recupera contenido ausente ni autentica un productor no confiable."
    },
    "schemaVsSemantics": "JSON Schema no valida orden ni joins/ausencias/relaciones. La validación semántica y el contexto fijado son obligatorios además del schema. KNOWN sólo indica proyección de hechos seguros presentes del primer throw del prefijo validado.",
    "interpretation": {
      "noDelta": "Sin EXTRA_KEY before: no calcular diferencia ni asegurar ausencia de ticket/send desde unafter1/1/1.",
      "afterExamples": "Counts2/1/1 o2/2/1 son efectosobservados parciales;2/2/2+non200 orienta retorno/prueba final después de efectos visibles al contador, sin autenticar receipts ni fijarMvsQA. Sólo registrar medidas; no clasificador de causa ni permiso de replay.",
      "historical": "CurrentDIAG1 sigue statusHTTP/countersUNKNOWN. Futuro200 sóloestablece esa muestra; sinW1automático ni transferir status a historia.",
      "task1": "No package completo fullTask1; todas lasSourceQualified/Task1Pass y7nonclaimsfalse. Esteplan no libera nuevo negocio."
    }
  },
  "finiteGet": {
    "component": {
      "bytes": 5761,
      "sha256": "10303c6098b54ab7c00cdf61f0b168783a0ff2283db75c79edc01202acb6f684",
      "blob": "4a98aa0c77c0d1eb61c5ba6ecabdbf6a4d72ec32"
    },
    "producer": {
      "world": "Use exact S08, S09 and S10 bound in current Source13. Unchanged choose assertion is at S08:18:143; S08:18:118 is historical only. Preserve separate notices POST assertion S08:41:12, original rejection, counts and settlements.",
      "labels": "S08 world created per original createFiniteCoupledOwnerWorld. Arm private one-use method label on entry to monitor()/noScope() before first await using closed-over main and world-local state, mark ready in finally upon its normal or exceptional end without replacing any outcome. Only public counts() consumes a ready label synchronously, once before the existing async read. All ordinary direct count(f), noFurther, repeated internal counts, subcase calls, other worlds and active!=main never provide a measurement. No module-global or last-id inference; overlapping/unconsumed rearm or public count during armed work poisons pending observer for this world; it may emit UNKNOWN or omit, never reassign old facts. On scope failure S08:111 cannot reach internal snapshot when choose throws; postaction public count remains the measurement. No alteration to D07 (which marks enter, takes counts once, marks settled, emits C2SOURCE).",
      "flow": "In labeled public counts only, use the very same detached rows from existing plain(f.stub.snapshot()) at historic S08:22, once. Compute original business counters normally; only upon their successful construction project on already-returned rows then emit at most one bounded marker before returning unchanged counters. Projection/format/console errors are observation-only (UNKNOWN safely, or absent); original snapshot/count rejection, throw value, and failure to create business counters retain original path. Do not use finally to perform a new read or to publish an initialized zero. No label in public counts after successfully consumed. No second projection or retry. No action/after call added.",
      "time": "FIRST checkpoint is after case14 action and at its settled counter, before case15 action. SECOND is after case15 action at its own settled counter, before case16. Neither is an atomic bracket around provider execution; if 15 passes/different assertion, second remains post-entire-action. In an exact failed GET sample noScope did not execute its subsequent snapshot/drop/POST/restore path. Even so the count may include asynchronously progressing operations."
    },
    "predicate": {
      "source": "S01:220–232 creates the Ticket, S00:192,483–499 separates Ticket from TicketUse and detects duplicate stages. BASE codec e9b66f68b6dbabbfecc46072949a0d5d9f059141:18–30 sorts copied object keys, :59,:70–71 defines map/tickets, :81–112 validates types/keys/semantics, :130–133 canonical decoding. S10:58 snapshot returns the existing list, S09:5 detaches/disposes. Projection measures returned rows, distinct from S00 admission/decision. Never apply S00 duplicate-action rejection to two distinct finite Tickets; seeing them is the subject of the measure.",
      "input": "Ordinary dense array of 1..512 exact length-two [string key,value] pairs, unique nonempty string keys <=1024 UTF8 bytes. At most 16 rows in owner-ticket: namespace (bases plus :use), exactly one owner-project-ref: row. Stop before decoding overbounds. Short length check first on long keys/raw to avoid allocating unbounded strings; ASCII patterns and UTF8 bounds. Other namespace values are opaque; do not decode, stringify or hash them. Invalid/missing/capped input always UNKNOWN. These observer-only bounds can reduce available observation; they do not restrict or modify the business read.",
      "classified": "For every owner-project-ref: key require exactly owner-project-ref:<lowerhex64>, canonical decode ProjectRef of string <=8192 UTF8 B, map.projectRef equals suffix. For every owner-ticket: row accept only owner-ticket:<lowerhex64> or same + :use. String <=8192B, decode Ticket or TicketUse by key class using unchanged codec (roundtrip exact; no loose JSON equality). Key suffix digest must equal decoded ticketHash. Never accept a noncanonical prefix match, unrecognized suffix, body/key mismatch, foreign linkage, duplicate, malformed row or decoder failure as zero. For every base Ticket require map.projectRef,preconnectionId,subjectHash,sourceRevision exact match, map.issuedAt<=createdAt<expiresAt<=map.expiresAt. The actual codec checks purpose, exact fields, types, hash/time/action/TTL. No wall-clock read or live authorization.",
      "anchors": "Require exactly one connection Ticket with null connectionRef and one notices Ticket with nonnull connectionRef. Require one canonical :use for each of those anchors (joined by hash; use.consumedAt>=base.createdAt and <base.expiresAt). Each other base must be action finite, connectionRef identical to the notices anchor. Every :use must join a unique canonical base and same valid consumption interval. Finite :use neither increments nor removes a Ticket. Missing anchor, absent/doubled map, orphan use, broken anchor binding or invalid remaining row invalidates the whole measure, even after seeing two valid finite records. No source read/clock to strengthen links. No latest-record pick.",
      "value": "Only after validating all candidate rows, count DISTINCT valid base ticket hashes with action finite among the returned snapshot from the labeled main world. 0 -> string \"0\", 1 -> \"1\", >=2 -> \"2+\". Base business caps/duplicate-stage protection retain original meaning. Empty snapshots, invalid anchors, missing markers and sample failure are UNKNOWN. This is a local snapshot projection. The result authenticates neither ticket ownership nor issue or commit by this request. No keys, handles, identity, record contents, source revision, raw timestamp, record hashes or independently linkable ticket fingerprints escape.",
      "currentWorld": "Bind both observations to the same existing world-local f.choice.projectRef (the already accepted notices form S08:41, unchanged through the C15 public counter) and f.source.sourceRevision from S08:62. Require exact lowerhex64/lowerhex40 and equality to the map fields. Only these two existing primitive properties are read from f; never touch handle/cookie/token, take a new snapshot or cache identity between observations. Missing/mismatched anchor yields UNKNOWN. Each snapshot ties all eligible tickets and uses to its own unique map. A common world/projectRef/revision is evidence of comparable scope; no stronger cross-snapshot preconnection continuity or causal claim."
    },
    "childWire": {
      "raw": "Use the same bounded child stdout. The current producer emits monitor as '# C2FT3 ' plus canonical JSON keys id,value and LF, and scope as '# C2FT4 ' plus keys id,value,w,s,h and LF. The publisher also accepts a canonical C2FT3 scope frame as count-only compatibility. A valid C2FT3 scope frame with a known bucket and the required ordered native/TAP/Source/journal joins may yield afterScopeMissing.reason JOINED_SNAPSHOT. It supplies no winner tuple, so getWinner remains UNKNOWN and an independently known HTTP observation is preserved. A canonical C2FT4 scope frame can supply the winner tuple subject to the existing eligibility, status and normalization checks. Each frame and LF is at most 96 ASCII bytes. Count value is a string 0, 1, 2+ or UNKNOWN. The existing stream framing, order, and duplicate rules apply across both formats, including two frames for the same scope ordinal. No raw frame or child stdout enters the public artifact.",
      "join": "Process two independent streams as existing C1 grammar: native Subtest/result/block ordinal pairs and top-level console stream. In console stream require canonical ordered unique valid C2SOURCE prefix up to relevant checkpoint with id/status/phase/code and three 0..3 integer counters. For C14 phase monitor; for C15 scope; pass→OK,fail→TEST_FAILED, aligned with native. In this ordered console stream, the candidate marker lies strictly between predecessor C2SOURCE and its own C2SOURCE (13/14 or 14/15). Ignore other ordinary console lines. Do not require Subtest adjacency or order relative to C2SOURCE. Counter area emits marker before D07 C2SOURCE; business calls emit none. Scan whole bounded buffer for duplicates and foreign/reversed/malformed typed records, no accepting a first valid out of conflicting candidates. Ignore nested YAML/stack/message/escaped fake tokens as candidates; if only a nested lookalike is present, real marker is missing. Unsupported framing/undecodable text/torn typed candidate, >96 bytes, duplicate/reordered/foreign/misbracketed typed markers or over two top-level candidates taint marker stream for both counts (HTTP independent). An absent marker for one label does not erase another valid marker. A closed before-prefix survives an unrelated later missing marker or journal fault; no claim that unseen events did not happen."
    },
    "http": {
      "gates": "Exact C1 native-format rules/scalar provenance and total priority from protocol59ab firstFailure.sourceProjection, retarget exclusively to ordinal15 C2T1_SCOPE_MISSING, phase scope, expected GET assertion S08:18:143, first14 pairs/actions/counts returned; case15 action.throw (AssertionError/ERR_ASSERTION) is first throw in valid prefix and precisely matched, own count.return, native15fail and canonical C2SOURCE15 required. E3 measured S08 and select separate site. No C1 source row exported again. Require single flat testCodeFailure/ERR_ASSERTION/AssertionError/strictEqual block, two top-level decimal integer scalars actual=100..599 except200 and expected=200 with no dup/nesting/type coercion. Include actual/expected and matching throwSequence only on KNOWN. Http does not depend on C2FT3, C2FT4 or snapshot anchors.",
      "priority": [
        "0 infrastructure/admission/custody/N2 fault, no normal outcome.",
        "1 First validated throw different → NOT_APPLICABLE EARLIEST_THROW_DIFFERENT. 2 prior native failure → NOT_APPLICABLE EARLIER_NATIVE_FAILURE. 3 target native pass and its action/count.return → NOT_APPLICABLE TARGET_PASSED, otherwise UNKNOWN JOURNAL_UNRESOLVED. 4 complete clean journal without throw → NOT_APPLICABLE NO_QUALIFYING_THROW, otherwise missing target/antecedent → UNKNOWN JOURNAL_UNRESOLVED.",
        "5 target count missing/not returned → UNKNOWN COUNTER_UNAVAILABLE; torn native → TRUNCATED_NATIVE; invalid UTF8/control/header → NATIVE_FORMAT_UNSUPPORTED; ambiguous native → AMBIGUOUS_EVIDENCE; absent exact ordered native prefix/target -> TARGET_NATIVE_UNAVAILABLE.",
